{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493401,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T02:37:05.198Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493401-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493401-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e– Other –\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493401-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493401-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAsk:\u003c/strong\u003e First-party / catalog \u003cstrong\u003enative Bitwarden support\u003c/strong\u003e in Grok Bot (and Cursor where vault access for agents is needed), so agents can use Bitwarden without fragile custom MCP / CLI glue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCurrent behavior:\u003c/strong\u003e Bitwarden is usable today only via hand-rolled MCP / stdio connectors and agent-managed vault workflows. That works but is brittle (auth, secrets paths, re-auth, platform differences) compared with catalog plugins.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProposed behavior:\u003c/strong\u003e Official Bitwarden connector or plugin (OAuth / API key as appropriate) in the Grok Bot / Cursor connector catalog, maintained like other first-party integrations, with clear mobile + desktop auth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhy:\u003c/strong\u003e Household and agent logins already live in Bitwarden; native support would remove a standing DIY MCP footgun and match how other SaaS connectors are shipped.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnvironment:\u003c/strong\u003e Reporter uses Grok Bot with Bitwarden MCP today (agent workflows). App version Gap for this FR (product ask, not a single-screen repro).\u003c/p\